---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="FAQ | Spigadolce" currentPath="/faq">
  <section class="page-header">
    <h1>Frequently Asked Questions</h1>
    <p>Everything you need to know about Spigadolce demonstrations</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="max-width: 750px; margin: 0 auto;">

    <h3 class="faq-category">The Demonstration</h3>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary class="faq-question">Do I need any cooking experience?</summary>
      <p class="faq-answer">Not at all. These demonstrations are open to everyone, from complete beginners to experienced home cooks. The aim is simply to share the technique and the tradition — there is no pressure and no performance required.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary class="faq-question">How long does a demonstration last?</summary>
      <p class="faq-answer">It depends on the format and the group, but most sessions last between one and a half and two hours. There is always time to watch, to try, to ask questions, and to sit together and enjoy what we've made.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary class="faq-question">What will I learn?</summary>
      <p class="faq-answer">You'll learn to shape traditional Pugliese pasta by hand — orecchiette, cavatelli, strascinati, troccoli and other forms — using the same techniques passed down through generations of Apulian women. I'll share the history and stories behind each form, and you'll leave with recipes to try at home.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary class="faq-question">How many people can attend?</summary>
      <p class="faq-answer">The group size depends on the setting. Intimate sessions in a private home work best with up to 8 people. Larger community events or cultural settings can accommodate more. I adapt the demonstration to the context.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary class="faq-question">What language are the demonstrations in?</summary>
      <p class="faq-answer">Demonstrations are conducted in English. I am a native Italian speaker and happy to switch between both languages if the group prefers — or to throw in the occasional word of dialect from Andria.</p>
    </details>

    <h3 class="faq-category">Attending a Session</h3>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary class="faq-question">Is there a charge to attend?</summary>
      <p class="faq-answer">No. All demonstrations and workshops are offered freely and with no commercial purpose. Spigadolce is not a business — it is an act of love for a tradition I do not want to see disappear.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary class="faq-question">How can I attend a demonstration?</summary>
      <p class="faq-answer">Get in touch via the Contact page. Demonstrations take place in private homes, at community events, and in cultural settings across London. I am always happy to hear from individuals, community groups, schools, libraries or cultural organisations who would like to host a session.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary class="faq-question">Can you come to our community group or event?</summary>
      <p class="faq-answer">Absolutely. I particularly enjoy working with community organisations, cultural centres, schools and libraries. If you are organising an event and would like to include a Pugliese pasta demonstration, please get in touch and I will do my best to make it happen.</p>
    </details>

    <h3 class="faq-category">Dietary Requirements</h3>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary class="faq-question">Can you accommodate allergies or dietary requirements?</summary>
      <p class="faq-answer">Yes — please let me know in advance and I will adapt the session accordingly. The pasta dough I use is made from durum wheat semolina and water only, with no eggs, so it is naturally vegan.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary class="faq-question">Is the pasta vegan?</summary>
      <p class="faq-answer">Yes. Traditional Pugliese pasta — orecchiette, cavatelli, strascinati — is made from durum wheat semolina and water alone. There are no eggs, no dairy. It is one of the oldest and most honest forms of pasta in Italy.</p>
    </details>

    <div class="faq-cta">
      <h3>Still have a question?</h3>
      <p>Drop me a message — I'm always happy to help.</p>
      <a href="/contact" class="btn-primary">Get in Touch</a>
    </div>

  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .faq-category {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    color: var(--color-gold);
    margin: 2.5rem 0 1rem;
    padding-bottom: 0.6rem;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--color-warm);
  }
  .faq-item {
    background: #fff;
    border-radius: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 0.8rem;
    box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.04);
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .faq-question {
    padding: 1.2rem 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1rem;
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
  }
  .faq-question::after {
    content: '+';
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    color: var(--color-gold);
    font-weight: 300;
    transition: transform 0.2s;
  }
  details[open] .faq-question::after {
    content: '−';
  }
  .faq-question::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }
  .faq-answer {
    padding: 0 1.5rem 1.2rem;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: #666;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }
  .faq-cta {
    text-align: center;
    padding: 3rem 2rem;
    background: var(--color-dark);
    color: #fff;
    margin-top: 3rem;
    border-radius: 12px;
  }
  .faq-cta h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  .faq-cta p {
    opacity: 0.8;
    margin-bottom: 1.2rem;
  }
</style>
